cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "Auditory-Oddball-Psychopy: cued auditory oddball task for OPM-MEG"
version: "v1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-15"
abstract: >-
  PsychoPy implementation of an active, cued auditory oddball task for OPM-MEG with
  simultaneous EyeLink eye tracking, used at the Scully Center for the Neuroscience of
  Mind & Behavior (Princeton Neuroscience Institute). Adapted from the FieldTrip NatMEG 2014
  auditory oddball tutorial. An arrow cue sets the response hand; 3-7 standard tones
  (1000 Hz) are followed by one deviant tone (1200 Hz), and the participant presses the
  index-finger button on the cued hand. Uses VPixx pixel-mode triggers and
  hardware-scheduled VPixx audio.
